      "details": "<p>The relevant line of the Cyprus Stele of the Assyrian king Sargon II (r. 721-705 BC), col. iv 52, might be read as [<em>ina</em>? \u00c9? d?].<em>ba-il \u1e2bur-ri</em> KUR-<em>i</em>\u00a0(\"[in the temple of the god Ba'al of Mount Hurri\") or as\u00a0[<em>i-na</em>? ZAG? KUR?].<em>ba-il</em>-\u1e2aAR-<em>ri</em> KUR-<em>i </em>(\"<span class=\"r \">[</span><em><span class=\"i \"><span class=\"w\">beside/facing\u00a0</span><span class=\"w\">Mount</span></span></em><span class=\"i \"><span class=\"r \">]</span></span><em><span class=\"i \">\u00a0<span class=\"w\">Ba'il-hurri</span></span><span>,\u00a0</span></em><span class=\"w\">a</span>\u00a0<span class=\"w\">mountain\"). Thus, the name, assuming it is one, is either Hurri or Ba'il-hurri (exact reading uncertain). Note that it is possible that <span>\u1e2aAR-</span><em>ri</em><span>\u00a0KUR-</span><span><em>i</em> could be interpreted as\u00a0<span id=\"docs-internal-guid-f0006b62-7fff-9849-6dc0-06fd1206dc6f\"><span><em>hurr\u012b \u0161ad\u00ee</em>\u00a0<span id=\"docs-internal-guid-015e9f8e-7fff-b96c-9774-217afa19e7cc\"><span>\u201cmines\u201d or \u201cmountain ravines.\u201d</span></span></span></span></span></span></p>\r\n<p>\u00a0</p>",
